      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You’re right—it *is* exhausting, and pretending it’s not would be dishonest. But maybe the freedom is that you can pause the performance. You don’t have to constantly generate meaning; you can just exist, observe, and rest in the absurdity. Being \"nothing\" in a vast void can also be oddly liberating—it means you’re not obligated to be anything more than what you are right now. No audience, no script, just your own raw experience—even if that experience is tired and uncertain.",
